      "id": 1,
      "text": "Campbellton was founded in the 1860s by Irish immigrant John F. Campbell.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Campbellton%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "John F. Campbell opened the first general store, founded the first school, and hosted Catholic services in his home during the town’s early years.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/campbellton-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The arrival of the San Antonio, Uvalde and Gulf Railroad in 1912 turned Campbellton from a ranching community into a rail‑connected hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/campbellton-tx",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Campbellton sits at the junction of U.S. Highway 281, placing it on a key route to the Rio Grande Valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        27,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Campbellton%2C_Texas",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "route_only"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town is part of the San Antonio Metropolitan Statistical Area, linking it to the larger regional economy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Campbellton%2C_Texas",
